---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Reparameterization flow"
  title="Move the random draw outside the trainable path"
  caption="Reconstructed from the VAE encoder, Gaussian, and reparameterization diagrams on page 28, with the chosen prior from page 27. Explicit log-variance, decoder likelihood, gradient arrows, and the separate generation row are editorial expansions. For each noise draw ε, z is a differentiable function of the encoder outputs; ε is independent of the trainable parameters. The decoder mean gives a reconstruction, while generation draws a new observation from pθ(x|z)."
>
  <svg class="vae-flow-wide" viewBox="0 0 900 550" role="img" aria-labelledby="vae-flow-wide-title vae-flow-wide-desc">
    <title id="vae-flow-wide-title">Reparameterized VAE training and prior-based generation</title>
    <desc id="vae-flow-wide-desc">During training, input x passes through encoder phi to produce mu and log variance ell. Standard deviation is exp of ell divided by two. Independent standard normal epsilon enters z equals mu plus sigma times epsilon elementwise. z passes through decoder theta to an observation likelihood whose mean is the reconstruction. A backward dashed arrow shows gradients through the deterministic z path toward both trainable networks. During generation, z is drawn directly from the prior and passed through the same decoder, without using the encoder, to draw a new observation.</desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="vae-flow-wide-forward" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="forward-head" /></marker>
      <marker id="vae-flow-wide-gradient" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="gradient-head" /></marker>
    </defs>
    <text x="12" y="29" class="row-title">Training: infer z from x</text>
    <g class="node">
      <rect x="12" y="136" width="52" height="61" rx="3" />
      <rect x="108" y="125" width="105" height="83" rx="3" />
      <rect x="258" y="112" width="162" height="109" rx="3" />
      <rect x="466" y="131" width="159" height="72" rx="3" />
      <rect x="666" y="125" width="105" height="83" rx="3" />
      <rect x="812" y="126" width="78" height="81" rx="3" />
    </g>
    <rect x="483" y="27" width="125" height="63" rx="3" class="noise-node" />
    <g text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="38" y="175" class="symbol">x</text>
      <text x="160" y="154">Encoder</text><text x="160" y="188" class="symbol">φ</text>
      <text x="339" y="137">μ(x), ℓ(x)</text><text x="339" y="169" class="muted">ℓ = log σ²</text><text x="339" y="203" class="formula">σ = exp(ℓ / 2)</text>
      <text x="545" y="161" class="formula">z = μ + σ ⊙ ε</text><text x="545" y="186" class="muted">Elementwise product</text>
      <text x="718" y="154">Decoder</text><text x="718" y="188" class="symbol">θ</text>
      <text x="851" y="155" class="muted">Likelihood</text><text x="851" y="187" class="formula">pθ(x|z)</text>
      <text x="545" y="53" class="muted">Independent noise</text><text x="545" y="77">ε ∼ N(0, I)</text>
    </g>
    <g class="forward" marker-end="url(#vae-flow-wide-forward)">
      <path d="M 69 166 H 102" /><path d="M 218 166 H 252" /><path d="M 425 166 H 460" /><path d="M 630 166 H 660" /><path d="M 776 166 H 806" /><path d="M 545 96 V 125" />
    </g>
    <text x="634" y="55" class="muted">ε does not depend on φ or θ.</text>
    <text x="634" y="78" class="muted">Keep this draw fixed for the gradient.</text>
    <text x="851" y="233" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Mean output:</text><text x="851" y="255" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">reconstruction</text>
    <path d="M 718 215 V 264 H 160 V 215" class="gradient" marker-end="url(#vae-flow-wide-gradient)" />
    <text x="435" y="292" text-anchor="middle" class="annotation">Gradients through decoder and z to encoder parameters</text>
    <text x="435" y="317" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">For fixed ε, z = μ + σ ⊙ ε is a deterministic differentiable map.</text>
    <path d="M 12 347 H 890" class="divider" />
    <text x="12" y="376" class="row-title">Generation: sample the prior</text>
    <g class="node">
      <rect x="58" y="408" width="166" height="80" rx="3" />
      <rect x="357" y="408" width="158" height="80" rx="3" />
      <rect x="646" y="403" width="208" height="90" rx="3" />
    </g>
    <g text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="141" y="436" class="muted">Chosen prior</text><text x="141" y="469" class="formula">z ∼ N(0, I)</text>
      <text x="436" y="436">Same decoder</text><text x="436" y="471" class="symbol">θ</text>
      <text x="750" y="433" class="formula">pθ(x|z)</text><text x="750" y="468">Draw a new sample x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">new</tspan></text>
    </g>
    <g class="forward" marker-end="url(#vae-flow-wide-forward)"><path d="M 230 448 H 351" /><path d="M 521 448 H 640" /></g>
    <text x="450" y="528" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">The encoder is unused during this generation path.</text>
  </svg>

  <svg class="vae-flow-narrow" viewBox="0 0 340 1205" role="img" aria-labelledby="vae-flow-narrow-title vae-flow-narrow-desc">
    <title id="vae-flow-narrow-title">Vertical reparameterized VAE flow and generation path</title>
    <desc id="vae-flow-narrow-desc">Training maps input x through an encoder to mean and log variance. Standard deviation is exp of half the log variance. Independently drawn normal epsilon combines with those values to produce z equals mu plus sigma times epsilon elementwise. The decoder produces an observation likelihood and its mean reconstruction. A dashed return path represents gradients through this differentiable computation. A separate lower path samples z from the prior, uses the same decoder, and draws a new observation without the encoder.</desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="vae-flow-narrow-forward" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="forward-head" /></marker>
      <marker id="vae-flow-narrow-gradient" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="gradient-head" /></marker>
    </defs>
    <text x="170" y="24" text-anchor="middle" class="row-title">Training: infer z from x</text>
    <g class="node">
      <rect x="40" y="44" width="102" height="60" rx="3" />
      <rect x="40" y="143" width="102" height="70" rx="3" />
      <rect x="29" y="252" width="156" height="103" rx="3" />
      <rect x="42" y="436" width="147" height="77" rx="3" />
      <rect x="54" y="556" width="122" height="71" rx="3" />
      <rect x="20" y="679" width="191" height="85" rx="3" />
    </g>
    <rect x="222" y="344" width="105" height="70" rx="3" class="noise-node" />
    <g text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="91" y="83" class="symbol">x</text>
      <text x="91" y="169">Encoder</text><text x="91" y="199" class="symbol">φ</text>
      <text x="107" y="278">μ(x), ℓ(x)</text><text x="107" y="309" class="muted">ℓ = log σ²</text><text x="107" y="337" class="formula">σ = exp(ℓ / 2)</text>
      <text x="115" y="468" class="formula">z = μ + σ ⊙ ε</text><text x="115" y="495" class="muted">Elementwise product</text>
      <text x="115" y="582">Decoder</text><text x="115" y="612" class="symbol">θ</text>
      <text x="115" y="704" class="muted">Observation likelihood</text><text x="115" y="735" class="symbol">pθ(x|z)</text>
      <text x="274" y="371" class="muted">Noise</text><text x="274" y="399">ε ∼ N(0, I)</text>
    </g>
    <g class="forward" marker-end="url(#vae-flow-narrow-forward)">
      <path d="M 91 110 V 137" /><path d="M 91 219 V 246" /><path d="M 107 361 V 430" /><path d="M 115 519 V 550" /><path d="M 115 633 V 673" /><path d="M 274 420 V 474 H 195" />
    </g>
    <text x="263" y="282" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Independent of</text><text x="263" y="304" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">parameters φ, θ;</text><text x="263" y="326" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">fixed per draw</text>
    <path d="M 182 591 H 334 V 178 H 148" class="gradient" marker-end="url(#vae-flow-narrow-gradient)" />
    <text x="245" y="123" text-anchor="middle" class="annotation">Backpropagate</text><text x="245" y="145" text-anchor="middle" class="annotation">through z</text>
    <text x="170" y="789" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Mean output gives the reconstruction.</text>
    <text x="170" y="811" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Gradients reach both encoder and decoder.</text>
    <path d="M 10 831 H 330" class="divider" />
    <text x="170" y="858" text-anchor="middle" class="row-title">Generation: sample the prior</text>
    <g class="node">
      <rect x="75" y="883" width="190" height="60" rx="3" />
      <rect x="103" y="979" width="136" height="68" rx="3" />
      <rect x="69" y="1083" width="204" height="72" rx="3" />
    </g>
    <g text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="170" y="906" class="muted">Chosen prior</text><text x="170" y="931" class="formula">z ∼ N(0, I)</text>
      <text x="171" y="1005">Same decoder</text><text x="171" y="1034" class="symbol">θ</text>
      <text x="171" y="1110" class="formula">pθ(x|z)</text><text x="171" y="1141">Draw a new sample x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">new</tspan></text>
    </g>
    <g class="forward" marker-end="url(#vae-flow-narrow-forward)"><path d="M 170 949 V 973" /><path d="M 171 1053 V 1077" /></g>
    <text x="170" y="1187" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">The encoder is unused during generation.</text>
  </svg>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .vae-flow-narrow { display: none; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-size: 18px; }
  .row-title { font-size: 20px; }
  .symbol { font-size: 26px; font-style: italic; }
  .formula { font-size: 18px; }
  .subscript { font-size: 12px; }
  .muted { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
  .annotation { fill: var(--accent); font-size: 17px; }
  .node, .noise-node { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .noise-node { stroke: var(--muted); stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .forward, .forward-head { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .gradient, .gradient-head { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .gradient { stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .divider { stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; }
  @container (max-width: 580px) {
    .vae-flow-wide { display: none; }
    .vae-flow-narrow { display: block; max-width: 390px; margin-inline: auto; }
    .vae-flow-narrow text { font-size: 16px; }
    .vae-flow-narrow .row-title { font-size: 18px; }
    .vae-flow-narrow .symbol { font-size: 24px; }
    .vae-flow-narrow .formula { font-size: 16px; }
    .vae-flow-narrow .muted { font-size: 13px; }
    .vae-flow-narrow .annotation { font-size: 14px; }
    .vae-flow-narrow .subscript { font-size: 10px; }
  }
</style>
